  "theorem": "If each refinement level multiplies all modes by an arbitrary common gauge c_n and each individual mode has relative error at most eta_n, every common c_n cancels from mode ratios. Differential drift accumulates multiplicatively between products of (1-eta_n)/(1+eta_n) and its reciprocal; wave-clock drift uses square roots."
